    0.31416       0.60      -0.38000001     -0.38000000     5.10e-09   holds
    0.47124       0.90      -0.38000000     -0.38000000     4.65e-09   holds
    0.78540       1.50      -0.38000000     -0.38000000     2.92e-09   holds
    1.57080       3.00      +0.39978348     -0.38000000     7.80e-01   BREAKS
    3.14159       6.00      +1.01624682     -0.38000000     1.40e+00   BREAKS

   below-threshold rows must all hold: PASS

================================================================================================
CHECK 4  the real correlation function, N=3 crosstalk
================================================================================================
  ||H||_2 = 0.830259. Rebuilding the kernel at this Lambda.
  ||L_ker||_1 = 2.716030, grid threshold pi/(6L) = 0.630645

      quantity                      value
  ------------------------------------------------------------
   F'(0) by central difference    -0.23653645
   int L_ker(t) F(t) dt           -0.23653644
   abs err                         9.475e-09

   PASS

================================================================================================
VERDICT
================================================================================================
   CHECK 1 Fourier inversion      pass
   CHECK 2 derivative extraction  pass
   CHECK 3 discretisation         pass
   CHECK 4 real correlation       pass

   The kernel is correct as built, and the discrete grid identity holds
   below pi/(6L) and breaks above it - so the band limit is real and not
   a coincidence of the test function. It is safe to sample tau ~ p and
   weight by ||L||_1 sign(L(tau)) inside twirl_cal, which is the next step:
   the fixed-T bias floor should vanish, and because the O(T^2) term is
   excluded by construction rather than by design resolution, the degree-2
   aliasing of v106 should go with it.

  Scope: numerical quadrature on a finite t-window (60/Lambda), trapezoid rule,
  one cutoff realisation. The constants C_0 and gamma_1 of their Appendix C are
  NOT reproduced here - only the kernel and the grid identity, which are what
  the twirl construction needs.
